course: dictionary
lesson: 6782
title: Oral: spoken or by mouth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Oral has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one. Most often it means spoken, not written. An oral test is done by talking, and an oral report is given out loud to the class.
explain: Oral can also mean to do with the mouth, or taken by mouth. «Oral rehydration sachets mix salts and sugar in water so the gut absorbs it well.» You mix the sachet into water and drink it, so oral means by mouth here.
explain: Look for clue words around it. If the sentence mentions a talk, a presentation or a question, oral means spoken. If it mentions teeth, gums, medicine or drinking, it means to do with the mouth or taken by mouth. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: Oral means spoken, not written.
fact: Oral also means to do with the mouth, as in oral hygiene, which is keeping your mouth and teeth clean.
fact: Oral medicine is taken by mouth and swallowed, not injected.
fact: In the UK, an oral is a speaking exam, especially in a foreign language.
fact: «Oral rehydration sachets mix salts and sugar in water so the gut absorbs it well; fizzy drinks and fruit juice can make diarrhoea worse.»
exercise: «She gave an oral report on volcanoes to the whole class.» What does oral mean here? | Drawn on a poster | Written neatly in a notebook | *Spoken aloud | Sent by email
exercise: The dentist says, «Good oral hygiene means brushing twice a day.» What does oral hygiene mean? | Writing your homework neatly | Cleaning the family car | *Keeping your mouth and teeth clean | Keeping your bedroom tidy
exercise: «The doctor said the medicine is oral, so swallow it with water.» What does oral mean here? | Rubbed onto the skin | Injected into the arm | Written on the label | *Taken by mouth
test: Ella has an oral French exam on Friday. What will she do in it? | Draw pictures of France | Sing a song with no words | *Speak French out loud | Write French words on paper
test: Which phrase means history told by people talking about their memories? | *Oral history | Ancient history | Written history | Picture history
exam: Maya's grandad talks about his childhood for her project, and she writes down his memories. What does oral mean in «oral history»? | Found in old books and maps | Written down in a diary | Filmed with a camera and edited | *Spoken, told by people talking about their memories
